NAME
    diff - compare a saved memory snapshot against current memory

SYNOPSIS
    diff <name> [<count>]

DESCRIPTION
    Compares a memory space snapshot previously captured with snapshot(1)
    under <name> against the current contents of that same memory space,
    listing addresses whose byte values changed (at most <count> entries,
    default 20, parsed as hex).

    The stored snapshot is not modified, so the same baseline can be
    compared repeatedly as execution advances.

EXAMPLES
    diff before
    diff before 50

EXIT STATUS
    0   Comparison printed (or usage/not-found message printed).
    1   No target attached, invalid argument, or session service fault.

SEE ALSO
    snapshot(1), search(1), mem(1), spaces(1)
